Package: daybook
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: all
Maintainer: Gautam Savasaviya <gautam4tech@gmail.com>
Installed-Size: @INSTALLED_SIZE@
Depends: python3 (>= 3.14), python3-gi (>= 3.56), python3-gi-cairo, gir1.2-gtk-4.0 (>= 4.22), gir1.2-adw-1 (>= 1.9), python3-dateutil
Recommends: gir1.2-gsound-1.0
Suggests: gnome-shell-extension-appindicator
Section: gnome
Priority: optional
Homepage: https://github.com/GautamSavasaviya/daybook
Description: personal work planner with a daily plan, timer and reminders
 Daybook replaces a paper notebook for work. It keeps PMS tickets, face-to-face
 requests and non-project work in one list, plans each day around your meetings
 and lunch, and carries unfinished work over automatically.
 .
 It tracks time with a focus timer, reminds you before meetings and when
 planned time is up, handles time off and emergency meetings, and produces a
 timesheet, a standup and weekly reports. Everything is stored locally in one
 SQLite file, with daily backups.
 .
 Notification buttons need the installed application; the tray icon needs the
 GNOME AppIndicator extension.
